# A stable name for the wireless uplink adapter.
#
# Without this the two radios race for wlan0. The onboard brcmfmac is a
# built-in driver that still has to fetch firmware from the rootfs, and the
# USB adapter's rtl8xxxu loads as soon as the device enumerates, so which
# of them registers its netdev first is genuinely not decided. The access
# point profile, the DHCP configuration and three nftables rules all name
# wlan0, and none of them would notice being pointed at the wrong radio
# until nothing worked.
#
# So the USB adapter is renamed out of the wlan namespace entirely. wan0 is
# a name the kernel never assigns, which leaves wlan0 free for the onboard
# radio whichever order they appear in: if the adapter registers first it
# is renamed away before the other one asks, and if it registers second it
# was never going to get wlan0 anyway.
#
# Matched on the USB ids rather than the driver, because a driver name is
# a property of the kernel version and these ids are a property of the part
# in the drawer. Add a line for a different adapter rather than widening
# this one.
SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2357", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0109", NAME="wan0"
